<p>A Moscow court ordered pre-trial detention for Oleg Roldugin, an investigative journalist with the independent newspaper Novaya Gazeta, a day after his arrest on charges tied to the alleged illegal use of personal data. The case centers on reporting methods that Russian authorities say broke the law. The articles note that Roldugin is known for investigations into alleged corruption involving senior Russian figures, including former President Dmitry Medvedev and Chechen leader Ramzan Kadyrov. The detention adds to the pressure on independent journalism in Russia, where authorities have tightened restrictions on media outlets since the full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022. For readers following world affairs, the case offers a clear example of how legal tools are being used against reporters working on sensitive public-interest investigations, with immediate implications for press freedom and what remains of Russia&#x27;s independent media space.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/xgiRlNfL-jCwAKEw9N-n2mZGFe_id78_9a4l9P95MpcRNvWhpkDTqkj4LSiqLZ5SnPOWcXYCdtUn5BHKBpTp5T372u2vCTviv_zEK21MflnBmdJRTkHbqo4gEOqC-_neASjQyhxu9aX9xjLlVHcBoZRqAW9ZoSTFe1j9u-tANPDSBtjflVplZYgiJlr_7b3jI1to-u5JYQiGBVoLiErNYZlWYj00xxlsKkpfMoVGG1rOL_NG0At9Smmq-5H2M6ftQZyHZmHKcA' alt='Oleg Roldugin, an investigative journalist for the independent Russian newspaper Novaya Gazeta, stands inside an enclosure for defendants before a court hearing in Moscow on April 10, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Court hearing: Roldugin appeared inside a defendants&#x27; enclosure during the Moscow court hearing on April 10, 2026, showing that the case had already moved from arrest to formal custody proceedings.</li><li>Outlet status: The sources describe Novaya Gazeta as an independent newspaper, making the detention notable as space for non-state media in Russia continues to shrink.</li><li>Reported targets: Roldugin&#x27;s previous investigations looked into alleged corruption involving Dmitry Medvedev and Ramzan Kadyrov, two high-profile figures in Russian politics.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Russian court: The court ordered Roldugin into pre-trial detention after his arrest, backing a case built around allegations that he illegally used personal data. (<a href='https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/04/10/moscow-court-orders-arrest-of-novaya-gazeta-journalist-on-personal-data-charges'>Meduza</a>)</li><li>Novaya Gazeta: Coverage presents the newspaper as an independent outlet whose reporter had investigated alleged corruption among top officials. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/russian-investigative-journalist-is-placed-in-pre-trial-detention'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Le Monde analysis: The case fits a broader crackdown on independent news outlets that has intensified since Russia launched its offensive on Ukraine in February 2022. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/10/russian-investigative-reporter-from-novaya-gazeta-placed-in-pre-trial-detention_6752300_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/10/russian-investigative-reporter-from-novaya-gazeta-placed-in-pre-trial-detention_6752300_4.html'>Russian investigative reporter from Novaya Gazeta placed in pre-trial detention</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/russian-investigative-journalist-is-placed-in-pre-trial-detention'>Russian investigative journalist is placed in pre-trial detention</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/04/10/moscow-court-orders-arrest-of-novaya-gazeta-journalist-on-personal-data-charges'>Moscow court orders arrest of Novaya Gazeta journalist on personal data charges</a> - meduza.io</li></ul>